5417] [17592186412490 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e6df6c0-c5fb-5993-9a0a-f13c5e1ee5eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412490 #edb/ref 1074 "An expression is a contradiction if it is always false, regardless of the inputs.\n\nBy completing the final column in the truth table below, we obtain the following:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∧Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nAccording to the table, $(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)$ \n$\\text{isn't}$\nalways false. Therefore, it \n$\\text{isn't}$\na contradiction." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216769" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1071 "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)$ is a contradiction.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways false. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na contradiction." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47f2ef05-063f-5c83-82af-b14b43aa298e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412491 #edb/ref 1074 "An expression is a contradiction if it is always false, regardless of the inputs.\n\nBy completing the final column in the truth table below, we obtain the following:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,A∧¬B\\,$ | $\\,(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nAccording to the table, $(¬A∧B)∧(A∧¬B)$ \n$\\text{is}$\nalways false. Therefore, it \n$\\text{is}$\na contradiction." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412492 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412492 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216907" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412492 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412492 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412492 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "480f94bc-0561-588e-b570-1657983e06e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412492 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operations:\n\n- First, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)]≡¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨\\text{c}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and a contradiction equals the original statement:\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨\\text{c}]≡¬(¬X∨¬Y)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬X∨¬Y)≡¬¬(X∧Y)\n$$\n\n- Finally,  we simplify the double negation:\n\n$$\n¬¬(X∧Y)≡X∧Y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n¬[(¬X∨¬Y)∨(¬Y∧Y)]≡X∧Y\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
